SUMMARY:Muppets Treasure Island (1996) [Open Caption Screening]
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:USA | 99 min | G | Dir. Brian Henson\n \n"The Muppets are bac
 k into action in another movie based on a novel written by Robert Louis S
 tevenson. Kermit the Frog and his colleagues go on a warfare against ruth
 less pirates. They also share their problem-solving journey on sea to res
 cue a treasure." - IMDB\n \n"Muppet Treasure Island confirms what The Mu
 ppet Christmas Carol suggested -- that the Muppet legacy\, that staple of
  childhood for two generations now\, really has been passed into capable 
 hands." - Rob Salem (Toronto Star)\n \nWatch the trailer here: https://y
 outu.be/-37gsH0ideE?si=gz9EOHTuiiH8DcMF \n\n \n \nFor information on a
 vailable assistive content for WUD Film screenings\, please visit the Ass
 istive Movie Screenings in the Marquee Theater page.  \nVisit our Infor
 med Moviegoing Resources page for links to resources that explore film ra
 tings and content alerts.\nThis event is intended for UW-Madison students
 \, faculty\, staff\, Wisconsin Union members and their guests. Anyone can
  become a Wisconsin Union member.\n\nhttps://union.wisc.edu/events-and-ac
 tivities/event-calendar/event/wud-film-presents-muppets-treasure-island-1
 996-open\n\nSource: WUD Film (The Marquee)
URL:https://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-
 film-presents-muppets-treasure-island-1996-open
