SUMMARY:Terminator 2: Judgment Day (1991)
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:US | 153 Min | R | DCP | Dir. James Cameron\n \nIn this seque
 l set eleven years after "The Terminator\," young John Connor (Edward Fur
 long)\, the key to civilization's victory over a future robot uprising\, 
 is the target of the shape-shifting T-1000 (Robert Patrick)\, a Terminato
 r sent from the future to kill him. Another Terminator\, the revamped T-8
 00 (Arnold Schwarzenegger)\, has been sent back to protect the boy. As Jo
 hn and his mother (Linda Hamilton) go on the run with the T-800\, the boy
  forms an unexpected bond with the robot.-Rotten Tomatoes\n \n"The key e
 lement in any action picture\, I think\, is a good villain. Terminator 2 
 has one\, along with an intriguing hero and fierce heroine\, and a young 
 boy who is played by Furlong with guts and energy." - Roger Ebert for the
  Chicago Sun-Times\n \nWatch the trailer here: https://www.youtube.com/w
 atch?v=BuBD2s2NmEM \n\n \n\n \n \nFor information on available assist
 ive content for WUD Film screenings\, please visit the Assistive Movie Sc
 reenings in the Marquee Theater page.  \nVisit our Informed Moviegoing 
 Resources page for links to resources that explore film ratings and conte
 nt alerts.\nThis event is intended for UW-Madison students\, faculty\, st
 aff\, Wisconsin Union members and their guests. Anyone can become a Wisco
 nsin Union member.\n\nhttps://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-
 calendar/event/wud-film-presents-terminator-2-judgment-day-1991\n\nSource
 : WUD Film (The Marquee)
URL:https://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-
 film-presents-terminator-2-judgment-day-1991
END:VEVENT
